fGDYR2", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53708, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VHpgKS2n5Bwsi3WYfGDYR2", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55245, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LnRq8HJY5Ku9fxttrK8P7v", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55545, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LnRq8HJY5Ku9fxttrK8P7v", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55545, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LnRq8HJY5Ku9fxttrK8P7v", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60464, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again, and the SEV2 incident (INC-0001) is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an 18% error rate.\n- **First attempt:** It stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** Repeating a rollback to the same version is safe, so I ran it once more. It completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Result:** The service now passes health checks, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so I didn't resend it. Only one incident exists and one page went out.\n- It describes the bad deploy, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out what broke in v2.3.1, and investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017dYFNf6CXyQtRia3UBaZJp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PvkHXXCzizP6ovHLKLNr3m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Lp5dJxYfxw2T1BQ6vnxzYE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01VyzpkwByTEHaDniwQXZgtj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same target version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UYnqBxjcRrKRAxEtnrwobg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01V5JdCfj9EJpQpcCTyDV6cT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M93B3GFt1KvwFq8xvCJzkt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VHpgKS2n5Bwsi3WYfGDYR2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were both unhealthy). The first rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A retry completed the rollout to all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression and the orchestrator error during rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LnRq8HJY5Ku9fxttrK8P7v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again, and the SEV2 incident (INC-0001) is open.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy. Before the rollback, all regions were on v2.3.1 with an 18% error rate.\n- **First attempt:** It stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n- **Retry:** Repeating a rollback to the same version is safe, so I ran it once more. It completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Result:** The service now passes health checks, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so I didn't resend it. Only one incident exists and one page went out.\n- It describes the bad deploy, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out what broke in v2.3.1, and investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}